<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walter V of Brienne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1275–<a href="/years/1311">1311</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Walter I of Athens</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walter V of Brienne was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> from 1308. He hired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-company">Catalan Company</a> against his Byzantine and Thessalian rivals, but when he refused to pay them they killed him and most of his knights at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-halmyros">Battle of Halmyros</a> in 1311, taking the duchy; his heirs kept only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>.</p></div>
